.TH REDACTOR 1 "September 2026" "Redactor 0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
redactor \- portable offline sensitive-data substitution and exact restoration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B Redactor-cli
.RB [ --user " NAME" ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Redactor performs no network or internet communication. Vaults, diagnostics,
temporary files and exports live inside the movable application folder.
Passwords are prompted without echo; never put passwords on the command line.
Close the graphical application before using the CLI.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B create, info, password
Create an analyst account, inspect its password age, or change its password.
.TP
.B reminder on|off
Set the optional 60-day password reminder.
.TP
.B import INPUT OUTPUT
Extract editable text. No sensitive matches is not an error.
.TP
.B scan INPUT PLAN
Write a sensitive JSON review plan containing candidates and near matches.
.TP
.B review PLAN
Use --original or --kind to select values; --state sensitive|insensitive,
--replacement TEXT, --starts OFFSETS or --add to edit the plan.
.TP
.B near PLAN IMPORTED ORIGINAL confirm|edit|deny
Explicitly resolve a near match. Edit requires --value TEXT.
.TP
.B redact PLAN OUTPUT --reviewed
Apply the reviewed plan and save reversible mappings before export.
.TP
.B restore INPUT OUTPUT --reviewed
Restore exact replacements. Optional --ids and --kind select a subset.
.TP
.B obfuscate INPUT OUTPUT --reviewed
Apply saved mappings, optionally selected by --ids or --kind.
.TP
.B lookup
Filter with --query or --kind; sort with --sort and --descending.
.TP
.B batch-update --find TEXT --replace TEXT
Preview changes to --field original|replacement|kind. Select --ids or --kind.
Add --apply only after reviewing the preview. Related domains and IP prefixes
must remain consistent; current replacements must match original lengths.
.TP
.B delete --ids ID... --confirm DELETE
Delete selected mappings and aliases. Alternatively select --kind TYPE.
.TP
.B flush --confirm FLUSH
Delete all mappings. Detailed audit history can still contain originals.
.TP
.B audit [--output FILE]
Read sensitive audit JSON. Output must be inside the portable folder.
.TP
.B purge-history --confirm PURGE
Remove active and imported audit history; retain a history-purged event.
.TP
.B export-db OUTPUT
Prompt for a separate export password. ZIP, compressed TAR, 7z/zip7 or RAR
contains an encrypted database plus SHA256SUMS and SHA512SUMS. RAR requires
a licensed native utility in tools/rar.
.TP
.B import-db INPUT
Verify hashes and open as a new database under the authenticated local user.
Raw legacy .vault backups are also supported.
.TP
.B help-doc user|errors|cli|license
Display bundled offline documentation.
.TP
.B databases, new-db TITLE
List database IDs or create a database under the current user.
.TP
.B --database ID
Global option selecting a database; default main.
.TP
.B merge SOURCE_ID... [--ids ID...] [--kind TYPE] [--conflict keep|incoming] [--apply]
Preview selected/all mappings from multiple databases; apply explicitly.
.TP
.B copy-mappings OUTPUT, paste-mappings INPUT [--apply]
Transfer reviewed mappings using a sensitive JSON file inside the portable folder.
.TP
.B workspace [--input FILE]
Open editable INPUT, WORK PRODUCT and substitutions panels. Tab switches focus;
F3 imports, F4 adds manual values, F5 scans, F6 applies, F7 restores, F2 exports, F1 helps, Ctrl-Q exits and locks. Ctrl-T inserts a table column separator.
.SH FILES
data/vaults contains encrypted accounts; data/logs/errors.jsonl contains
sanitized diagnostic categories; data/tmp contains temporary work; exports
contains explicitly saved outputs. Move the complete folder while closed.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Detection requires human review. Length means Unicode character count,
not rendered width. Exports reconstruct text, not original document layout.
IP equality and binary common-prefix lengths and literal domain suffix
relationships are retained; geolocation, ordering and numeric distances are not.
Surrogate addresses must never be used as network targets.
Audit records contain sensitive originals. Checksums are not signatures;
this application is not an externally certified chain-of-custody system.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success. 2 indicates an error with a stable R001-R011 or R999
reference, recommended action and Error Guide section. argparse usage errors
also return 2.
.SH SEE ALSO
Run "Redactor-cli help-doc errors" for recovery instructions and
"Redactor-cli help-doc cli" for examples. Use "man ./redactor.1" without installation.
